      "narrative": "The baseline MLP achieved a training accuracy of 78.47% versus a test accuracy of 66.15%. This 12.33-point gap indicates moderate overfitting, which is characteristic of training an unscaled 180-dimensional feature space without dropout or weight regularisation. The test accuracy (66.15%) substantially exceeds the 25% random-guess baseline, confirming the primary hypothesis. The confusion matrix reveals that the top misclassification occurred between 'happy' and 'fearful' (16 instances). Furthermore, mutual confusion between acoustically tense pairs (fearful vs disgust: 12 errors) was compared with distinct pairs (happy vs fearful: 20 errors), partially moderating the acoustic similarity hypothesis. In the context of SDG 3 / Target 3.4 (mental health triage), 'fearful' recall stands at 75.7%; reducing missed distress false negatives remains the critical objective for Phase 2 normalisation."
